-- title:
--   Lemma 33 — Hoeffding's inequality uniformly over sample sizes and at a predictable random time
-- statement:
--   Let $Z_1,\dots,Z_T$ be i.i.d. real random variables with values in $[a,b]$ almost surely, and write $\mathbb E[Z]$ for their common mean. For every $\delta>0$ the following two statements hold.
--
--   1. With probability at least $1-\delta$, simultaneously for all $1\le T'\le T$,
--   $$
--   \frac1{T'}\sum_{i=1}^{T'}Z_i-\mathbb E[Z]\le(b-a)\sqrt{\frac{\log(T/\delta)}{2T'}}.\qquad\text{(A.1)}
--   $$
--   2. Let $\tau$ be a random variable with values in $\{1,\dots,T\}$ such that, for every $t\in\{1,\dots,T\}$, the event $\{\tau\le t\}$ is determined by $Z_1,\dots,Z_{t-1}$ (for $t=1$: it is trivial). Then with probability at least $1-\delta$,
--   $$
--   \frac1{\tau}\sum_{i=1}^{\tau}Z_i-\mathbb E[Z]\le(b-a)\sqrt{\frac{\log(T/\delta)}{2\tau}}.\qquad\text{(A.2)}
--   $$
--
--   The price of uniformity over all $T$ sample sizes is the factor $T$ inside the logarithm. The second statement lets an algorithm decide adaptively when to stop sampling and still use Hoeffding's bound at the random time it stops.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The bound is one-sided, as printed. The variables are indexed by $1,\dots,T$, mutually independent, each with the law of $Z_1$. "$\mathbb I\{\tau\le t\}$ is a measurable function of $Z_1,\dots,Z_{t-1}$" is measurability of $\{\tau\le t\}$ for the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $Z_1,\dots,Z_{t-1}$. Probabilities are real numbers (`μ.real`).
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: Z₁, …, Z_T i.i.d. with a generic copy Z, mean E[Z] → Z i for i ∈ {1, …, T} mutually independent, each identically distributed with Z 1; E[Z] = ∫ Z 1; reason: the notes' E[Z] is the common mean; same instances
--   - encoding: I{τ ≤ t} is a measurable function of Z₁, …, Z_{t−1} → {τ ≤ t} is measurable for the σ-algebra generated by Z₁, …, Z_{t−1} (trivial at t = 1); reason: a {0,1}-valued function is σ(Z₁..Z_{t−1})-measurable iff it is a measurable function of Z₁..Z_{t−1} (Doob–Dynkin); same instances
--   - encoding: T ≥ 1, implicit (a sample Z₁, …, Z_T) → T ∈ ℕ; reason: at T = 0 no instance changes: (A.1) quantifies over an empty range and no τ takes values in the empty [T], so both claims hold trivially
--   - encoding: δ ∈ (0, 1), implicit → δ > 0; reason: for δ ≥ 1 the probability bound 1 − δ ≤ 0 is trivial; only δ ≤ 0, where log(δ⁻¹) is undefined, is excluded
-- source:
--   Foster & Rakhlin, Foundations of Reinforcement Learning and Interactive Decision Making, arXiv:2312.16730v1, Lemma 33, (A.1)–(A.2), p. 156

import Mathlib
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace FoundationsRL.TailBounds

/-- **Lemma 33** (Hoeffding's inequality with adaptive stopping time). For i.i.d. `Z₁, …, Z_T`
with values in `[a, b]` almost surely, with probability at least `1 − δ`,
`(1/T′) ∑_{i=1}^{T′} Z_i − E[Z] ≤ (b − a) √(log(T/δ)/(2T′))` for all `1 ≤ T′ ≤ T` (A.1).
As a consequence, for any random `τ ∈ [T]` such that for all `t ∈ [T]` the indicator `I{τ ≤ t}`
is a measurable function of `Z₁, …, Z_{t−1}`, with probability at least `1 − δ`,
`(1/τ) ∑_{i=1}^{τ} Z_i − E[Z] ≤ (b − a) √(log(T/δ)/(2τ))` (A.2).
Foster & Rakhlin, *Foundations of Reinforcement Learning and Interactive Decision Making*,
arXiv:2312.16730v1, Lemma 33, (A.1)–(A.2), p. 156.

**Formalization Note.** The variables are `Z i` for `i ∈ {1, …, T}` (the values of `Z` at other
indices play no role); they are mutually independent and each has the law of `Z 1`, so
`E[Z] = ∫ Z 1`. The bound is one-sided, as printed. "`I{τ ≤ t}` is a measurable function of
`Z₁, …, Z_{t−1}`" is `{τ ≤ t}` measurable for the σ-algebra generated by `Z₁, …, Z_{t−1}`
(the trivial σ-algebra at `t = 1`). `δ > 0` is the only restriction on `δ`; for `δ ≥ 1` both
claims are trivial. Probabilities are `μ.real`. -/
theorem lemma_33 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    (T : ℕ) (Z : ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (hindep : iIndepFun (fun i : Finset.Icc 1 T => Z i) μ)
    (hid : ∀ i ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, IdentDistrib (Z i) (Z 1) μ μ)
    (a b : ℝ) (hab : ∀ i ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, Z i ω ∈ Set.Icc a b)
    (δ : ℝ) (hδ : 0 < δ) :
    1 - δ ≤ μ.real {ω | ∀ T' ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T,
        (1 / (T' : ℝ)) * ∑ i ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T', Z i ω - ∫ ω', Z 1 ω' ∂μ ≤
          (b - a) * Real.sqrt (Real.log ((T : ℝ) / δ) / (2 * (T' : ℝ)))} ∧
    ∀ τ : Ω → ℕ, (∀ ω, τ ω ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T) →
      (∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T,
        MeasurableSet[⨆ i ∈ Finset.Ico 1 t, MeasurableSpace.comap (Z i) inferInstance]
          {ω | τ ω ≤ t}) →
      1 - δ ≤ μ.real {ω |
        (1 / (τ ω : ℝ)) * ∑ i ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (τ ω), Z i ω - ∫ ω', Z 1 ω' ∂μ ≤
          (b - a) * Real.sqrt (Real.log ((T : ℝ) / δ) / (2 * (τ ω : ℝ)))} := by sorry

end FoundationsRL.TailBounds
